  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nardostachin may exert its biological effects on SMMC-7721 through multiple distinct pathways. The first pathway involves Nardostachin acting as a target for Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is targeted by 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, ultimately leading to the inhibition of SMMC-7721. The second pathway involves Nardostachin directly targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by Cassialactone, also leading to the inhibition of SMMC-7721. These two pathways are distinct in their molecular targets but both result in the same downstream effect on SMMC-7721. The scores from the different paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship between Nardostachin and SMMC-7721, with the highest score in the first and third paths suggesting a stronger association. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Nardostachin to modulate SMMC-7721 through different molecular mechanisms, contributing to its biological activity.",
